    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d74">

                <pb facs="0254" n="82" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg82"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/4443</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The German Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bernstorff</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-01-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 10, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: Under instructions of my
                    Government I beg to transmit to you the enclosed memorandum, concerning the new
                    offensive armament of the merchant vessels of our enemies. I am further directed
                    by my Government to discuss this matter with you and to add to the memorandum
                    that it, of course, does not cancel the pledges given by my Government in the
                    note of May 4, 1916.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d74-f1"/>
                </p>
                <pb facs="0255" n="83" xml:id="pg83"/>
                <p>I should be very much obliged to you for an appointment as soon as you have been
                    able to study a translation of the enclosed memorandum and are prepared to
                    discuss it with me.</p>
                <p>I further beg to enclose a cipher message for the Foreign Office in
                        Berlin,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d74-f2"/> which refers to the above-mentioned
                    question and to your note of December 18 last concerning peace terms.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d74-f3"/> I should be very grateful for kind transmission to
                    Berlin.</p>
                <p>With many thanks in advance, I remain [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Bernstorff</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d74-a1.xml" xpointer="d74-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d74-a2.xml" xpointer="d74-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
